WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.500
Vibe coding made pull requests cheap.

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.900
Reviewing them still isn’t.

3
00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:09.100
What if AI made you better,
not just faster?

4
00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:15.700
First, read the project’s rules.

5
00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:19.300
Every rule, quoted from its source.

6
00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.700
Check the issue is still yours.

7
00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:28.900
Agents do the legwork,
on your own machine.

8
00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.500
Answer first.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.300
Then see the explanation.

10
00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.700
Which way would you do it?

11
00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:43.300
Taste grows by weighing trade-offs.

12
00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:48.100
Stuck on a line? Ask about it.

13
00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.500
Before it ships, explain it back.

14
00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.700
Missed something? Fix it in a line.

15
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:02.500
Predict what the maintainer will ask.

16
00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.300
Your words. The project’s rules.

17
00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.700
And what you didn’t test.

18
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:15.700
One Draft PR. Then stay for the review.

19
00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.100
Learn from what they actually said.

20
00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:28.000
From vibe coding to knowing why.
